Steps: (1) Give the button an ID in XML (android:id="@+id/login_button"). (2) In the Activity's onCreate, setContentView(R.layout.activity_main). (3) Find the view: val loginButton: Button = findViewById(R.id.login_button). (4) Set listener: loginButton.setOnClickListener { val intent = Intent(this, SecondActivity::class.java); startActivity(intent) }. If SecondActivity is a new activity, declare it in AndroidManifest.xml inside the <application> tag: <activity android:name=".SecondActivity"/>. No special permissions required for simple activity navigation. Example snippet: 
class MainActivity : AppCompatActivity() {
  override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
    super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
    setContentView(R.layout.activity_main)
    val loginButton: Button = findViewById(R.id.login_button)
    loginButton.setOnClickListener {
      startActivity(Intent(this, SecondActivity::class.java))
    }
  }
}
